.TH VAROOM 1
.SH NAME
varoom \- pseudo-3D road racing game
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B temple/varoom
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Varoom
is a port of the TempleOS racing game.
It runs under
.IR wm (1).
.PP
The view is from behind your car, looking down the road.
The course is a closed circuit of straights and curves that
rises and falls in dips, with red and white shoulder stripes,
bushes on the surrounding land, and seven purple opponent cars
circulating at speed.
A minimap in the bottom-right corner shows the track in yellow
with your car as a light-cyan dot and the opponents as
light-purple dots.
The heads-up line at the top left shows the percentage of the
lap completed, the elapsed time, and the best time, which is
kept across runs.
.PP
Steer and accelerate with the arrow keys.
Going off the road slows the car; touching another car ends the
game.
Complete the lap to win \(em finishing faster than the best time
is saluted with a beep.
.PP
The controls are:
.TF space
.TP
.B Left / a
Steer left
.TP
.B Right / d
Steer right
.TP
.B Up / w
Accelerate
.TP
.B Down / s
Brake
.TP
.B Enter / r
Restart
.TP
.B Esc / q
Quit
.PD
.SH FILES
.TF /lib/temple/sprites
.TP
.B /lib/temple/sprites
vector bush sprites
.TP
.B /fonts/temple/temple.font
the 8x8 system font used for the heads-up text
.SH SOURCE
.B /appl/temple/varoom.b
